//! BSC condition mask semantics (chosen for this emulator; pinned
//! here authoritatively per saga step 11):
//!
//! ```text
//! mask bit | meaning when set
//! ---------+-----------------------------------------------------
//! 0x01     | Z   -- ACC == 0
//! 0x02     | -   -- ACC < 0 (high bit set, sign-magnitude)
//! 0x04     | +   -- ACC > 0 (sign-magnitude positive, nonzero)
//! 0x08     | E   -- ACC even (low bit clear)
//! 0x10     | C   -- carry indicator set
//! 0x20     | O   -- overflow indicator set
//! ```
//!
//! BSC short: tests the displacement byte as the mask. If any
//! masked condition matches, **skip** the next instruction (advance
//! IAR by that instruction's word size). Mask = 0 means no
//! condition tested -> never skip.
//!
//! BSC long: tests the low 6 bits of the address word as the mask.
//! If any masked condition matches, **skip** (do not branch -- IAR
//! is already past the long-form instruction). If no masked
//! condition matches, **branch** to the address. Mask = 0 means no
//! condition -> always branch (the codegen's unconditional-branch
//! shape).
//!
//! ACC sign is tested in **two's-complement** terms (the natural
//! interpretation; the historical 1130 used sign-magnitude, which
//! diverges only at the value 0x8000 for `+` vs `-`. Two's-comp
//! makes "+/-/Z" partition cleanly).

